    "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR refactors non-ISA specification handling to use the standardized `spec_text` schema pattern instead of the previously used `tagged_text` format. The `spec_text` pattern is already used throughout other UDB schemas (CSR, instruction, extension, etc.) and allows content to be either a simple Asciidoc string or an array of conditional text objects with optional `when()` expressions.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Updated non-ISA schema to reference `spec_text` instead of `tagged_text` for description and section content\n- Modified Ruby rendering logic in `NonIsaSpecification` to handle the simplified content structure (no `id` or `normative` fields)\n- Migrated `preface_demo.yaml` data file to the new format, removing `id` and `normative` fields from content statements\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 3 out of 3 changed files in this pull request and generated 1 comment.\n\n| File | Description |\n| ---- | ----------- |\n| spec/schemas/non_isa_schema.json | Updated schema to use spec_text reference for description and section content fields, removing references to tagged_text |\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/udb/obj/non_isa_specification.rb | Simplified render_structured_prose method to handle spec_text format without id/normative fields; accepts strings and conditional_text hashes |\n| spec/custom/non_isa/preface_demo.yaml | Migrated content from tagged_text format to spec_text format, removing id and normative fields from statements |\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/riscv/riscv-unified-db/new/main/.github/instructions?filename=*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
